WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:07.819
This automotive case investigates steering
judder during braking, separating brake

00:00:07.819 --> 00:00:16.368
excitation, wheel balance, steering resonance
and sensor installation. Local Qwen3 Coder 30B

00:00:16.368 --> 00:00:22.500
follows a preselected operator measurement
plan on synthetic data.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:31.429
RAG retrieves the setup and quality documents,
including sensor roles, installation notes,

00:00:31.429 --> 00:00:38.630
the invalid-code rule and calibrated disc
inspection method. Documents guide

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:42.800
interpretation; native measurements test it.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:51.411
The workflow reviews complete-source quality,
masks the documented invalid wheel-speed code

00:00:51.411 --> 00:00:59.531
on a derived channel and verifies the actual
output while preserving raw data. It does not

00:00:59.531 --> 00:01:03.050
invent an undocumented unit correction.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:11.545
Braking and coast are compared at the same
measured wheel speed. Physical-encoder order

00:01:11.545 --> 00:01:19.733
tracking supplies 1X amplitudes using the same
amplitude convention, helping distinguish

00:01:19.733 --> 00:01:22.990
speed effects from braking effects.

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:30.548
Independent sensors, the repeat recording and
calibrated disc-thickness measurements provide

00:01:30.548 --> 00:01:36.695
separate evidence. Resonance amplification
alone does not identify the exciting

00:01:36.695 --> 00:01:41.830
component; the assessment separates excitation
from amplification.

00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:49.611
FL disc-thickness variation is 0.030 mm versus
the 0.015 mm fixture limit. At 798.732 rpm,

00:01:49.611 --> 00:01:56.663
native 1X peak amplitudes are 0.205628 g
during braking and 0.00411901 g during coast.

00:01:56.663 --> 00:02:03.306
After operator corrections, the assessment
separates likely brake excitation from

00:02:03.306 --> 00:02:10.030
possible steering-response amplification.
Physical confirmation remains necessary.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:19.720
The video ends with the latest exported report
from this run, showing actual analysis plots,

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:27.596
numerical tables, citations and the
assessment. The adjacent report link opens

00:02:27.596 --> 00:02:29.010
this same PDF.
